  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1237 PM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThere is little change in the weather pattern with high pressure \nover the Desert Southwest dominating the pattern. Troughing to the \nnortheast has pushed increased winds aloft farther south over the \ncentral areas of eastern Utah and Western Colorado. With the clear \nskies across the region and strong diurnal heating, look for stronger \nwinds gusting to 30 mph across the Gunnison Basin and the northern \nSan Juans this afternoon which, combined with the very dry \nconditions with relative humidity in the single digits, is \ngenerating critical fire weather conditions. Hence a Red Flag \nWarning is in effect from noon through 8 PM this evening for these \nareas. Though the gusty winds in other areas across the northern \nareas are more marginal not warranting a warning, understand that \nlocalized areas of critical fire weather conditions will occur \nacross the region. Exercise extra care if you are out in the forest \nor wilderness areas today. Over the next couple days, the high \npressure will build, spreading north and east over the region. This \nwill put a damper on the winds, but look for temperatures soaring to \nabout ten degrees above normal reaching record territory again. \nIssued a Heat Advisory for Friday and Saturday from 1 PM to 8 PM in \nthe Grand Valley in Colorado and the lower valleys of southeastern \nUtah from I-70 corridor south. It is wise to avoid being out in the \nsun during the hottest part of the day. Drink plenty of water, wear \nlight clothing and take regular breaks from strenuous activities.\n\nLooking out in the longer term, the deterministic models are \nsuggesting some low-level moisture sneaking up under the high Sunday \ninto early next week. Guidance is picking up on this moisture, \nincreasing the clouds to reduce the diurnal heating and cool \ntemperatures a bit, but the ensembles are less optimistic, keeping \nthe high entrenched over the Southwest barring the door to the \nmoisture. There's not a lot of confidence either way, so stay\ntuned.",
